SUMMARY:Comedy on the River - A Unique Paddle-in Comedy Show! 
DESCRIPTION:Toronto SUP\, Kayak & Canoe Adventures - Meetup Group\n**Come 
 Enjoy our Comedy On The River show on Friday June 19th!** To book your spo
 t\, please go to the link:\n[https://torontoadventures.ca/all-adventures/c
 omedy-shows-on-the-river/](https://torontoadventures.ca/all-adventures/com
 edy-shows-on-the-river/)\n\nLink will show live boat availability and opti
 ons!\n\n**Kayak or Canoe or Standup Paddle Board your way to a Comedy show
  right on the Humber River!**\n\nJoin us for laughter-filled evenings with
  talented comedians while enjoying the beautiful scenery of the Humber Riv
 er. Looking to try something truly unique?! Our super popular Comedy On Th
 e River paddle in comedy shows are back again for another season!\n\nLocat
 ed on Toronto’s beautiful Humber River our Comedy On The River event sta
 rts at our Humber Paddling centre which is only a 5-minute walk from Old M
 ill TTC Station! Upon arrival\, we’ll get you signed in and set you up w
 ith your boat and equipment before you embark on your scenic paddle of the
  meandering Humber River to our Comedy Show located right on the river! Up
 on arrival you’ll be greeted by host Dan Galea\, and some of Toronto’s
  biggest upcoming comedians!\n\n**Pricing (per boat)\, Payable online thro
 ugh:**\n**[https://torontoadventures.ca/all-adventures/comedy-shows-on-the
 -river/](https://torontoadventures.ca/all-adventures/comedy-shows-on-the-r
 iver/)**\n\n* Single Kayak (seats 1 person) : $40 +taxes\n* Tandem Kayak (
 seats 2 people) : $80 +taxes\n* Regular Canoe (seats 2 people) : $70 +taxe
 s\n* Large Canoe (seats 3 people) : $90 +taxes\n* Stand Up Paddleboard (1 
 person) : $45 +taxes\n* Voyageur Canoe Seat (1 person): $40 +taxes\n* Brin
 g Your Own Boat (boat/equipment): $10 +taxes\n\n**What's Included:**\n\n* 
 Boat(s)\n* Paddle(s)\n* PFD(s) “Lifejackets”\n* A comedy show right on
  the river!\n* Our friendly staff to help you every step of the way!\n\n**
 What to Bring:**\n\n* Dress for the weather!\n* Wear closed-toes athletic 
 footwear you don't mind getting wet or muddy.\n* Blanket to keep you cozy 
 during the show.\n* Snacks & Drinks (Non Alcoholic)\n* Government issued p
 hoto ID.\n\n**Important Information:**\n\n* Check specific event dates for
  start time and duration!\n* Anyone under 18 must be accompanied by an adu
 lt or legal guardian.\n* We Start & Finish this event at our Humber Locati
 on\, so no need for a shuttle.\n* Plan to arrive at least 15 minutes early
  for Check-In to ensure that you get out on time and enjoy the whole show.
 \n* Waivers to be signed on location.\n* Paddlers must be comfortable trea
 ding water while wearing a PFD and reaching a shoreline (minimum 20 metres
  to shore).\n\n**Cancellation & Weather**\n\n* *Events are subject to weat
 her and other factors out of our control. Any weather cancellations will b
 e announced through email to booked attendees and on the home page of www.
